{"When evt.destinationCalendar is null, undefined, or an empty array, mainHostDestinationCalendar becomes undefined. Accessing .integration on undefined throws a TypeError. The condition needs optional chaining: mainHostDestinationCalendar?.integration": 0.9744385480880737, "The fallback branch uses event.destinationCalendar?.find((cal) => cal.externalId === externalCalendarId) when externalCalendarId is falsy. Since this branch only executes when externalCalendarId is falsy, the find condition searches for cal.externalId === undefined/null, which will never match a valid calendar. This should use mainHostDestinationCalendar?.externalId instead": 0.992935836315155, "The condition for setting slug directly on the organization was inverted from !IS_TEAM_BILLING_ENABLED to IS_TEAM_BILLING_ENABLED. Previously, slug was set directly only when billing was disabled. Now it's set when billing is enabled, which contradicts the intended behavior where paid organizations should use requestedSlug in metadata pending approval": 0.9487632513046265, "When neither eventType.destinationCalendar nor organizerUser.destinationCalendar exists, evt.destinationCalendar is set to null. The subsequent evt.destinationCalendar?.push(...teamDestinationCalendars) does nothing due to optional chaining on null. This silently discards all team members' destination calendars for collective events": 0.9984002709388733, "The credential fetching logic (querying prisma.credential.findUnique with app.slug include, then constructing a credential object) is duplicated verbatim in both createAllCalendarEvents and updateAllCalendarEvents. This ~25 line block should be extracted into a shared helper function": 0.12616029381752014, "The check if (!Array.isArray(hosts)) on line 746 is unreachable dead code. The variable hosts is initialized with eventType.hosts || [] on line 744, which guarantees it's always an array": 0.5183485746383667}